; How deeply each function nests, counted on the parsed tree rather than on
; indentation: every `match`, `function`/`fun`, `try`, `if`, `while` and `for`
; that encloses an expression is one level, and a function bound by `let` costs
; none, so naming an inner step is what flattens a deep function. Past five
; levels fails and five warns (CONTRIBUTING.md, "Keep nesting shallow").
; `just check-nesting` runs it
; over the hand-written OCaml under lib/, bin/ and tools/, and tests/nesting/
; holds its output on small fixtures to checked-in expectations.
(executable
 (name nesting)
 (modules nesting)
 (libraries compiler-libs.common))
